  "tagline": "A Redis-protocol database on RocksDB that trades a little latency for disk-sized capacity.",
  "description": "Kvrocks implements the Redis protocol on top of RocksDB, so data lives on SSD with RAM used for caching rather than holding the full dataset. Originally built at Meitu and now an Apache top-level project, it supports most Redis data types, Lua, transactions, namespaces and a cluster mode managed by a controller. Recent versions add a search engine over JSON and hashes. It fits workloads that outgrew Redis's memory budget but still want the Redis API, at the cost of disk-bound latency.",
